        "body": "Equifax Inc. is a public company headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia, and trades under the ticker EFX, according to its profile. Its website describes it as a credit bureau that provides credit reports and credit scores to businesses and consumers, along with identity protection tools offering daily monitoring and alerts. The site describes a product called Equifax Complete and says that dedicated ID Restoration Specialists work on a customer's behalf to help them recover if they become a victim of identity theft.\n\nMuch of the site's content is educational. It covers how financial behavior affects credit and what appears on credit reports, warning signs of fraud and identity theft and steps to take after a theft, how debt affects credit scores, choosing and managing credit cards, personal finance and saving, and types of loans including personal and student loans and co-signing. The site also offers Spanish-language material covering Equifax credit reports in the United States, credit scores, and money management tips.\n\nThe profile lists no AI products and no MCP servers for the company. It records 103 law exposure matters in Georgia, and no lawsuits are listed.",
